# ORM

## Framework semantics

The CakePHP ORM centers on Tables, Entities, associations, `SelectQuery`, finders, and marshaling via `newEntity`/`patchEntity`. Tables are the default interface for application domain data — not ad-hoc `Connection::execute` / PDO.

## Required behavior

- Prefer Table/ORM APIs for ordinary reads and writes; treat raw Connection SQL as exceptional (`orm-vs-connection-sql`).
- Compose queries; prefer custom finders for reusable semantics.
- Prefer Query expressions and bindings over string SQL fragments.
- Prevent N+1 with deliberate `contain` / join strategies.
- Distinguish filtering associations (`matching` / joinWith) from eager loading (`contain`).
- Do not assume bulk updates (`updateAll` / query `update`) run entity callbacks/rules.

## Anti-patterns

- Hidden N+1
- Over-eager contain
- Bypassing ORM for convenience
- Unsafe SQL concatenation
- Eloquent-style mental models (not Laravel)

## Review checklist

- [ ] Query composable and intentional
- [ ] Association loading justified
- [ ] Lifecycle implications understood for writes
- [ ] No unnecessary Connection/raw SQL for domain CRUD
